// Day 26 - dependency call breakdown: time spent in SQL, Service Bus, and any
// outbound HTTP, per operation.
//
// Question this answers: when a request is slow, where is the time actually
// going - inside the app's own code, or waiting on something external? `type`
// distinguishes the dependency kind (SQL, Azure Service Bus, HTTP, etc - exactly
// what OpenTelemetry's SqlClient instrumentation and the Azure SDK's own Service
// Bus activity source report, see host/Capstone.Web/Program.cs). `target` is the
// specific downstream (a SQL server FQDN, a Service Bus namespace) - useful once
// there is more than one of a given type.
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| summarize
    CallCount = count(),
    AvgDurationMs = round(avg(duration), 2),
    P95DurationMs = round(percentile(duration, 95), 2),
    SuccessRatePercent = round(100.0 * countif(success == true) / count(), 1)
    by DependencyType = type, Operation = name, Target = target
| order by DependencyType asc, CallCount desc
